---
import WriteupLayout from "../../layouts/WriteupLayout.astro";
import LabelledBlock from "../../components/LabelledBlock.astro";

const title = "Culture Clash: Omer Ali Omer";
const description =
  "Project write-up: AI fusion recipes across 28 cuisines with Google Gemini, built by a team of five at GreatUniHack 2025.";
---

<WriteupLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  name="Culture Clash"
  meta="Next.js · TypeScript · Google Gemini · GreatUniHack 2025"
  icon="/work-culture-clash.png"
>
  <Fragment slot="links">
    <a
      href="https://github.com/Git-Push-Chill/CultureClash"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/Git-Push-Chill/CultureClash</a
    >
  </Fragment>

  <LabelledBlock label="Problem">
    <p class="writeup__lede">
      Pick two food cultures and the app blends them into a fusion recipe,
      drawing on 28 cuisines.
    </p>
    <p>
      Built with a team of five, Aun Raza, Ibraheem Iqbal, Anas Bataweel,
      Ismail Shafie and me, at GreatUniHack 2025. For the result to be
      usable it has to be structured, not free-form text: recipes with
      ingredient-origin tracking, plus generated flag imagery for each
      pairing.
    </p>
    <p>
      The goal, straight from the project brief we wrote ourselves: bridge
      cultural divides through food, using AI to generate fusion recipes
      across cuisines rather than just listing them side by side.
    </p>
  </LabelledBlock>

  <LabelledBlock label="Decisions">
    <p>
      Next.js 15 and TypeScript end to end. Google Gemini does the
      generation, returning structured recipes with ingredient-origin
      tracking rather than plain text.
    </p>
    <p>
      Engineered properly despite the hackathon time box: API caching with
      TTLs, rate limiting, and error boundaries, plus full keyboard and
      screen-reader accessibility.
    </p>
    <p>
      We split the work based on expertise: myself and Aun worked on the
      front end, Ibraheem worked on the back end, Anas worked on
      integrations and the API, and Shafie was the team's presenter.
    </p>
    <p>
      There's no live deployment: the repo is the only link.
      Deployment to Vercel was planned but the clock ran out before submission.
    </p>
  </LabelledBlock>

  <LabelledBlock label="What I'd do differently">
    <p>
      We'd spend more time on design thinking, properly fleshing out the
      pre-build activities before jumping into code. Future work would add
      more social features: sharing, recipe ratings and community recipe
      submissions, which would mean adding user authentication and accounts.
    </p>
  </LabelledBlock>
</WriteupLayout>
